  {
    "id": "eca58aa72bad81326e6d",
    "source": "Open Game Master bundles game content from the System Reference Document 5.1 (SRD 5.1) by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC-BY-4.0).",
    "sourceHash": "eca58aa72bad81326e6d3b7784ed176c1bb6bdcd1ecfaeb4bf5bc6bb7d276620",
    "kinds": [
      "jsx-expression"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/app/licenses/page.tsx",
        "line": 38
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "970c1abe95f26357ded2",
    "source": "Open Game Master is a Dungeons & Dragons 5e table where an AI sits in the Dungeon Master's chair, or a friend does with the AI as their assistant. You and your friends play the adventurers. The app is the rulebook and the dice.",
    "sourceHash": "970c1abe95f26357ded2ff5f4afe190eddd524227aff3404b14826ba2d548639",
    "kinds": [
      "localized-call"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/components/HowToPlayDialog.tsx",
        "line": 38
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "2c203e9889a5eafb4269",
    "source": "Open Game Master is a self-hosted, multiplayer Dungeons & Dragons 5e platform run by an AI Game Master. Server admins manage users, models, images, voice and campaign plugins from the Admin panel. Game content comes from the SRD 5.1 and Open5e; see",
    "sourceHash": "2c203e9889a5eafb4269bc7a31ce3f6562aef3d158d4ec79210126d67f2f1ca0",
    "kinds": [
      "localized-call"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/components/HelpDialog.tsx",
        "line": 260
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "10be32c5d8562e95e7b4",
    "source": "Open Game Master is an open source (MIT licensed), self-hosted application. You run it on your own server, or on your own phone or computer, and your data stays there. The creator of Open Game Master does not collect, sell, or share any user data, and has no access to the data on any server or device running the app. The one exception is described under \"Sharing a world from your device\" below.",
    "sourceHash": "10be32c5d8562e95e7b449a0de633fb1972fec51ac35fbb4fa4891632cd3a904",
    "kinds": [
      "jsx-expression"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/app/privacy/page.tsx",
        "line": 23
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "ff37c3aa934a5efd42d2",
    "source": "Open Game Master is open source (MIT licensed), self-hosted software. There is no hosted service to sign up for, no company behind it, and no account with the project itself. You download the code and run it on hardware you control. These terms explain what the software is, what it is not, and who is responsible for what.",
    "sourceHash": "ff37c3aa934a5efd42d20707222825fb93a40967d6c897a859e22a194c7ba050",
    "kinds": [
      "jsx-expression"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/app/terms/page.tsx",
        "line": 23
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "df8ae54b809d04f776bf",
    "source": "Open Game Master itself is MIT licensed. Homebrew content belongs to the user who created it, and installed campaign plugins belong to their authors.",
    "sourceHash": "df8ae54b809d04f776bf3b063143958ed0b8bf93082ecce9f7306e2bb063f6a0",
    "kinds": [
      "jsx-expression"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/app/licenses/page.tsx",
        "line": 123
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "653be04e3520d461555b",
    "source": "Open Game Master stores only the information needed to run your server, in a local database on your machine:",
